+//! A doubly linked list implemented with raw pointers and `unsafe`.
+//!
+//! # Invariants
+//!
+//! * Every node is heap allocated exactly once (via `Box`) and owned by the
+//!   list it is linked into.
+//! * `front` is `Some` iff `back` is `Some` and `len > 0`.
+//! * For a node `n` linked into the list:
+//!   - `(*n).next` is the node following it (or `None` at the back),
+//!   - `(*n).prev` is the node preceding it (or `None` at the front),
+//!   - if `(*n).next == Some(m)` then `(*m).prev == Some(n)`, and vice versa.
+//! * `len` equals the number of linked nodes.
+//! * A node is deallocated exactly once, either when it is removed from the
+//!   list or when the list is dropped.
